1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,199
This is a fictional student diary for the Kanqual demonstration.

2
00:00:04,549 --> 00:00:06,793
The voice is synthesized.

3
00:00:07,143 --> 00:00:08,567
I'm Maya.

4
00:00:08,917 --> 00:00:11,711
I'm in my second year at Alderbridge.

5
00:00:12,061 --> 00:00:21,184
If you had asked me last fall whether I belonged here, I probably would have said yes, because I thought that was the answer I was supposed to give.

6
00:00:21,534 --> 00:00:24,793
I had the scholarship and the campus sweatshirt.

7
00:00:25,143 --> 00:00:30,001
But I ate lunch looking at my phone so nobody would notice I was sitting alone.

8
00:00:30,351 --> 00:00:35,270
Last week I went to A Seat at the Table, the first-generation lunch.

9
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:38,639
The poster said, come on your own.

10
00:00:38,989 --> 00:00:41,993
That sounds small, but it mattered.

11
00:00:42,343 --> 00:00:45,907
Usually I assume everyone will arrive with friends.

12
00:00:46,257 --> 00:00:53,145
I stood outside Room 104 for a minute, and a student at the door asked whether I wanted to sit with her.

13
00:00:53,495 --> 00:00:57,334
She didn't ask me to introduce myself to the whole room.

14
00:00:57,684 --> 00:01:00,198
We talked about office hours.

15
00:01:00,548 --> 00:01:04,392
I admitted I used to think you could only go if you were failing.

16
00:01:04,742 --> 00:01:08,526
Two other people laughed because they had thought the same thing.

17
00:01:08,876 --> 00:01:15,314
It was the first time that not knowing an unwritten rule didn't feel like evidence that admissions had made a mistake.

18
00:01:15,664 --> 00:01:18,648
I saw one of them in the library yesterday.

19
00:01:18,998 --> 00:01:23,051
They moved their bag and made space for me before I even asked.

20
00:01:23,401 --> 00:01:26,260
That's what belonging feels like to me now.

21
00:01:26,610 --> 00:01:29,209
Somebody expects you to be there.

22
00:01:29,559 --> 00:01:33,568
You're not starting from zero every time you walk into a room.

23
00:01:33,918 --> 00:01:35,777
It isn't everything.

24
00:01:36,127 --> 00:01:41,451
There's a Founders' Evening coming up, and forty-five dollars is my grocery money.

25
00:01:41,801 --> 00:01:44,970
I don't own formal clothes, either.

26
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:51,058
I can feel included at lunch and still feel that another part of the university isn't meant for me.

27
00:01:51,408 --> 00:01:53,327
Both things are true.

28
00:01:53,677 --> 00:01:56,831
I'm going to the garden welcome day on Sunday.

29
00:01:57,181 --> 00:01:59,780
I don't know anything about gardening.

30
00:02:00,130 --> 00:02:05,329
The flier says tools are provided, which takes away one thing to worry about.

31
00:02:05,679 --> 00:02:09,237
Maybe I'll ask the person from the library to come.

32
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:11,811
I think that's the change.

33
00:02:12,161 --> 00:02:16,010
I'm starting to invite people instead of waiting to be invited.